 "intro": "By the river Silarus in Lucania, 71 BC, at the end of the slave war. You are Marcus Licinius Crassus, given command after Spartacus has beaten several Roman armies.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s and Appian’s accounts, Crassus restored discipline by decimating a cohort that had fled, then built a trench and wall across the toe of Italy. Spartacus broke through on a snowy night, and his army split; Crassus destroyed a group of Gauls and Germans, then met Spartacus near the Silarus. Spartacus killed his horse before the battle and died trying to reach Crassus. Six thousand prisoners were crucified along the Appian Way. Pompey, arriving from Spain, caught some fugitives and claimed credit. The other choices are what-ifs.",
